WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.634
-Right-wing conspiracy theories

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.267
about Russia's invasion
of Ukraine

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.868
have spun wildly out of control,

00:00:05.868 --> 00:00:07.834
as Donald Trump,
leader of the Republican Party,

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.267
declared that,
if he were president,

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.534
he would threaten to use nukes
against Russia.

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.734
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:18.234
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:18.234 --> 00:00:20.567
We're all familiar
with the alternate universe

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.267
of lies and conspiracy theories

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.701
Republicans have spread
about the 2020 election.

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:27.200
Trump's gang of weirdos
keeps popping up

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.100
to repeat those lines
every chance they get.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.234
Over the weekend,
MyPillow CEO Mike Lindell

00:00:31.234 --> 00:00:32.667
was wandering around the grounds

00:00:32.667 --> 00:00:34.234
at a Trump rally
in South Carolina,

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:37.767
rattling off a list of states
Trump had supposedly won,

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:40.234
but were stolen from him
because of voter fraud.

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:41.601
-You know where the most votes

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.534
in the United States
were stolen?

00:00:43.534 --> 00:00:44.901
Anyone want to guess?
-Texas?

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.167
-California.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:49.868
1.5 million votes were stolen
from Donald Trump.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:51.167
Donald Trump won --
You want to hear

00:00:51.167 --> 00:00:52.534
what states we know he won?

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.133
Here's the states
that Donald Trump won for sure.

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:58.734
He won Minnesota, Wisconsin,

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:03.167
Michigan, Pennsylvania,
New Hampshire, Georgia.

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:06.467
No. Georgia, Arizona,
and Nevada.

00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:08.467
He probably -- We don't know,
but he might've won Maine.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.601
He might've won Colorado.

00:01:09.601 --> 00:01:11.067
There's four others in question.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.234
-Are there any states
Trump didn't win?

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.367
[ As Lindell ]
He won Wisconsin, Minnesota,

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:18.067
Pennsyldonia, Old Jersey,

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.934
New Jack City,
Arrakis, Endor, Xanadu,

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:23.200
and the one that has
the flag with

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.467
da bear.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:27.901
Also, dude, if you're going
to ask people

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.767
to guess something, give them
a second to answer, first.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.400
[ Laughter ]
The guy didn't get
the microphone back to his mouth

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:35.267
before you yelled it out.

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:36.801
Guess which hand
has the jelly bean.

00:01:36.801 --> 00:01:38.834
It was this one, but I also
have one in this one.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:40.567
Oh, wait, it's gone.
Somebody stole it!

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:42.167
No, wait.
I remember I ate it.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:44.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.033 --> 00:01:46.667
But this fringe,
paranoid thinking is not unique

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.868
to the 2020 election.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:49.167
As we've discovered

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:51.434
during Russia's horrific
invasion of Ukraine,

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.133
right-wing pundits have become

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:55.501
increasingly unhinged
in their conspiracy theories

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.367
about the war
and Biden's response.

00:01:57.367 --> 00:01:59.534
Over the weekend,
Fox host Maria Bartiromo,

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:02.100
one of the most pro-Trump
voices on TV,

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.167
suggested that it was Joe Biden

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.000
who saw Vladimir Putin
as a partner

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.267
and didn't want to confront him.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.534
-Some people have told me,
over the weekend,

00:02:09.534 --> 00:02:11.667
that they feel that,
at the end of the day,

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:15.467
this administration
does not see Putin as the enemy.

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.267
They see him as a partner,
on many issues.

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.834
They see him as a partner
on climate change.

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:24.100
They see him
as a partner on the Iran deal.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.968
When is this administration
going to get serious

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:31.234
in telling Vladimir Putin,
"We are done with partnerships"?

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:33.968
That means no Iran deal,
walk away,

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:37.400
no more renegotiating
on America's behalf,

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.701
no more products from Russia!

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:41.467
-No more products?!
We've already banned

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.934
Russian oil, vodka,
diamonds, and seafood.

00:02:43.934 --> 00:02:45.100
I mean, what else is there?

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.868
[ As Bartiromo ]
No more products from Russia!

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:48.334
No more Russian ballet,

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.100
no more Russian salad dressing,

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:52.868
and no more of those
little Russian dolls!

00:02:52.868 --> 00:02:55.334
[ Laughter ]
Biden keeps saying
he's going to ban them,

00:02:55.334 --> 00:02:57.000
but then,
every time you open one up,

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.667
there's another one inside.

00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:01.334
When?
When does it end, Joe?!

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:05.334
Let's just go back
to this part for a minute.

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:08.000
-Some people have told me,
over the weekend --

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.400
-Alright, that sentence
right there is how you know

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:10.767
you're about to hear
some [bleep]

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:12.834
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.667
First of all,
you're kicking things off

00:03:14.667 --> 00:03:17.067
with some unsourced
weekend gossip?

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.968
That's how my writers start off
their Monday morning excuses.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.801
"Some people, over the weekend,
told me that,

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:25.801
if you smash two edibles
together, they, um,

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:26.934
cancel each other out.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.367
[ Laughter ]
But I think they were wrong

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.467
and that's why I'm late

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:30.701
and all my clothes are wet
and -- Wait.

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:31.601
These aren't my clothes.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.834
What on Earth
are you talking about?

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:37.501
You think Biden sees Putin
as a partner?

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.868
First of all,
Trump is the one who called

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.467
Putin's invasion of Ukraine
savvy and genius

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:44.667
and desperately lavishes praise
on Putin every chance he gets.

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:46.834
Trump was clearly the one
who saw Putin as a partner,

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.868
although, I'm not sure Putin
felt the same way.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.801
Based on Putin's face
when they were together,

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:53.634
Putin saw Trump as a competitor

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.601
who was way too easy
to outsmart.

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.667
[ Laughter ]
Putin always had the smile
of a spelling bee contestant

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:01.100
after the other kid
got a super hard word.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.300
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.634
"Your word is insouciant,"

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:04.934
[ As Trump ]
Insouciant? We love --

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.334
We love insouciant,
don't we, people?

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:07.367
[ Laughter ]
We love it.

00:04:07.367 --> 00:04:08.567
It's a great word.
We love it

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.334
because it starts with an "I."
We know that.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.200
And then, right after that
comes the "N"

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.434
and, at that point,
at that point,

00:04:15.434 --> 00:04:16.567
you've basically spelled it.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:20.467
You've bas--
And isn't that enough?

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.834
I feel like can we just leave it
there and get full credit?

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:24.400
[ Buzzer ]
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.501
And they can't even seem

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.367
to keep their conspiracy
theory straight.

00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.400
One day, Biden, supposedly,
sees Putin as a partner

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:33.334
and then, next, they claim Biden
somehow orchestrated

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.601
this whole thing
as a way to continue

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:38.234
accumulating power
as COVID subsides.

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:40.133
-You wonder if,
looking backward,

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:42.868
many years from right now,
historians will notice

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:45.133
the remarkable coincidence
in timing.

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:47.501
Have you noticed?
Here it is.

00:04:47.501 --> 00:04:50.334
At exactly the moment
when the emergency powers

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:54.601
they awarded to themselves
to fight COVID started to wane,

00:04:54.601 --> 00:04:57.167
our leaders began pushing
for conflict with Russia

00:04:57.167 --> 00:05:00.100
and then, on the basis
of that conflict,

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:03.467
they assumed
historic war powers. Hm!

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:06.133
Virtually no one has paused
to ask him- or herself

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:07.701
where this might be going.

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.701
How long until our leaders
do something similar

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.200
to their domestic enemies here
in the United States?

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:15.100
How long before they accuse you
of collusion or disloyalty,

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:16.934
or some other
hard-to-define crime,

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:18.100
declare you an enemy
of the state,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.834
and then confiscate
your bank account?

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:22.534
-[ As Carlson ]
How long before they declare you
an enemy of the state

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:24.133
and confiscate
your bank account?

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.534
How long until they take away

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.868
your 15% friends and family
discount at Ruby Tuesday's?

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:31.100
[ Laughter ]
Even though your cousin
worked there

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:32.200
for an entire summer.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:33.734
And how long
before they tell you

00:05:33.734 --> 00:05:35.334
you can't go
to Ruby Tuesday's anymore,

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:36.868
you can only go
to Ruby Monday's,

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:39.334
[ Laughter ]
even though it's your
constitutional right

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.834
to go to Ruby's any day
of the week?

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.968
And how long
before the waitress tells you

00:05:42.968 --> 00:05:44.367
you can't have an Oreo shake

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:46.367
because that's something
that only exists at Applebee's?

00:05:46.367 --> 00:05:48.834
[ Laughter ]
And how long after you
politely suggest

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:50.767
they just put Oreos
into a blender does she say,

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:52.934
"Can we please not have
this conversation again?"

00:05:52.934 --> 00:05:55.234
[ Laughter ]
And after you push past her
and run to the kitchen

00:05:55.234 --> 00:05:57.200
with the Oreos you have hidden
in your pocket,

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:59.167
with the full intention
of making your own,

00:05:59.167 --> 00:06:00.801
are you wrestled to the ground

00:06:00.801 --> 00:06:04.434
by a teenage busboy who is way
stronger than he looks?

00:06:04.434 --> 00:06:09.033
[ Laughter ]
And how long before that busboy
looks in your eyes and says,

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:11.601
"I worked with your cousin.

00:06:11.601 --> 00:06:13.367
He was a dickhead, too"?

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:14.133
How long?

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:17.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.701 --> 00:06:21.567
Of course, the reality is that
Biden has tried

00:06:21.567 --> 00:06:24.133
to delicately thread the needle
between supporting Ukraine

00:06:24.133 --> 00:06:26.067
and severely punishing Russia,
on the one hand;

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.767
while resisting calls
for more direct

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:29.400
military intervention,
on the other.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.667
Because a direct military
conflict with Russia,

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:33.734
a nuclear power, could
potentially be catastrophic,

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:35.968
a point Biden himself made
on Friday,

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:37.167
in typical Biden fashion.

00:06:37.167 --> 00:06:38.434
-We're going to continue

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:40.200
to stand together
with our allies in Europe

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.567
and send
the unmistakable message

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:46.567
that we will defend every inch
of NATO territory --

00:06:46.567 --> 00:06:48.667
every single inch --

00:06:48.667 --> 00:06:51.400
with the united,
galvanized NATO.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.534
One movement.

00:06:52.534 --> 00:06:55.033
But, look, the idea --

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:57.701
the idea that we're going
to send in offensive equipment

00:06:57.701 --> 00:07:00.167
and have planes and tanks
and trains

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:04.067
going in with American pilots
and American crews,

00:07:04.067 --> 00:07:06.767
just understand,
don't kid yourself.

00:07:06.767 --> 00:07:08.501
No matter what you all say,

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:12.934
that's called
World War III, okay?

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:17.133
Let's get it straight
here, guys.

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:19.567
That old expression,
"Don't kid a kidder."

00:07:19.567 --> 00:07:21.167
-[ As Biden ]
Hey, turn the mic way up

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:23.334
because I'm going to do
that spooky whisper thing.

00:07:23.334 --> 00:07:26.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.634
Yeah, jack it way up.

00:07:27.634 --> 00:07:28.934
I'm going to get in close.

00:07:28.934 --> 00:07:30.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:32.267
And what do you mean?
Are you the kidder

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:34.567
in this situation
and who are you trying to kid?

00:07:34.567 --> 00:07:36.667
You sound like you're buying
a used car

00:07:36.667 --> 00:07:38.567
at a Ford dealership
in Scranton.

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:40.167
[ Laughter ]
"This is a beauty.
It's a 2013 Fiesta.

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:42.200
It only has 300,000 miles
on it."

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.467
[ As Biden ]
Hey, pal, don't think

00:07:43.467 --> 00:07:45.200
you could jerk my chain
like that.

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:47.667
[ Laughter ]
Don't kid a kidder.
Don't piss on my leg

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:49.067
and tell me it's raining, okay?

00:07:49.067 --> 00:07:50.367
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.367 --> 00:07:52.367
Now, give me the car
for five bucks and a handshake

00:07:52.367 --> 00:07:54.367
and we'll call it even.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:55.834
Biden is right --
the situation in Ukraine

00:07:55.834 --> 00:07:57.968
is a humanitarian emergency

00:07:57.968 --> 00:08:00.601
and we should do everything
possible to support Ukraine

00:08:00.601 --> 00:08:02.434
and help the millions of people
who are suffering,

00:08:02.434 --> 00:08:04.667
but any direct military conflict
with Russia

00:08:04.667 --> 00:08:07.634
would threaten to quickly spiral
out of control

00:08:07.634 --> 00:08:09.634
into a world war
between nuclear powers,

00:08:09.634 --> 00:08:10.667
and no one wants that.

00:08:10.667 --> 00:08:12.334
I mean,
am I the only person here

00:08:12.334 --> 00:08:14.100
who grew up [bleep] terrified
of nuclear war?

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:16.467
What else is coming back
from the '80s, He-Man?

00:08:16.467 --> 00:08:18.334
[ Laughter ]
Oh, it is? Alright, sweet.

00:08:18.334 --> 00:08:20.133
The point is Biden is right,
which is why

00:08:20.133 --> 00:08:22.534
politicians and the media need
to be extremely careful

00:08:22.534 --> 00:08:24.601
when discussing forms
of escalation that sound good,

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:27.133
but would actually be
extremely bad,

00:08:27.133 --> 00:08:29.067
like, for example,
a no-fly zone.

00:08:29.067 --> 00:08:32.701
If NATO and the U.S. declare
a no-fly zone over Ukraine,

00:08:32.701 --> 00:08:36.033
we would then have to enforce it
by shooting down Russian planes,

00:08:36.033 --> 00:08:38.367
at which point we'd be in a war
with a nuclear power.

00:08:38.367 --> 00:08:40.100
And, when you explain that
to people,

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:41.934
it suddenly becomes
much less appealing,

00:08:41.934 --> 00:08:44.234
as CBS discovered in a new poll
over the weekend.

00:08:44.234 --> 00:08:45.634
-A new CBS News poll shows

00:08:45.634 --> 00:08:49.234
59% of Americans support
a no-fly zone,

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:52.000
though the support drops to 38%

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.734
when Americans consider that it

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:56.400
could be taken as an act of war.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.367
-That's right,
support for a no-fly zone drops

00:08:58.367 --> 00:09:01.567
by over 20 points, once people
actually understand what it is.

00:09:01.567 --> 00:09:03.100
It's like conducting a poll
where you ask people...

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:08.200
[ Laughter ]
And then you follow
with a second poll, ask them...

00:09:09.634 --> 00:09:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.467 --> 00:09:13.734
"Free chicken nugget!
Don't finish! Hold on!

00:09:13.734 --> 00:09:17.000
Dude, good news!
What's the second part?"

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.501
[ Laughter ]

00:09:18.501 --> 00:09:19.868
I think it goes without saying
that this is

00:09:19.868 --> 00:09:21.167
a very precarious moment

00:09:21.167 --> 00:09:22.901
in which reckless
military escalation

00:09:22.901 --> 00:09:24.434
could lead
to even more catastrophe.

00:09:24.434 --> 00:09:26.734
We need to help the millions
of people who are suffering

00:09:26.734 --> 00:09:29.801
and support diplomatic paths
toward an end to the conflict.

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.934
Even Ukraine's president
has said the only way

00:09:31.934 --> 00:09:33.400
to end the war is
through dialogue.

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:35.901
The last thing we need right now
is, say, I don't know,

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:37.701
a former president
bragging that,

00:09:37.701 --> 00:09:39.234
if he were still in office,
he would threaten

00:09:39.234 --> 00:09:40.634
to use nuclear weapons and --

00:09:40.634 --> 00:09:44.300
Wait. Oh, why am I positing such
an insane hypothetical?

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:46.334
Oh, [bleep]
We have a Trump clip coming up,

00:09:46.334 --> 00:09:47.467
